From 85e5e09f63829390b2c44d580f8c2fd61caed268 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chengyi Zhao <zhaochengyi@uniontech.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 13:42:46 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix: start filter-chain with PipeWire after relogin

filter-chain.service was only pulled in by default.target. Since the
user manager may remain active across logout/login, default.target is
not re-triggered and the service stays stopped after PipeWire restarts.

Add pipewire.service as an additional WantedBy target so the filter
chain is automatically pulled in whenever PipeWire starts, matching the
behavior of wireplumber.service.
---
 src/daemon/systemd/user/filter-chain.service.in | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/daemon/systemd/user/filter-chain.service.in b/src/daemon/systemd/user/filter-chain.service.in
index 542cbd7..a614cd0 100644
--- a/src/daemon/systemd/user/filter-chain.service.in
+++ b/src/daemon/systemd/user/filter-chain.service.in
@@ -17,5 +17,4 @@ Restart=on-failure
 Slice=session.slice
 
 [Install]
-Also=pipewire.socket
-WantedBy=default.target
+WantedBy=pipewire.service
-- 
2.20.1

